WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.989 --> 00:00:05.180
When a permission that has been granted on
a resource is no longer needed, it should

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.640
be revoked.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.120
People who have permission on a resource when
that permission is not needed are a risk for

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.990
doing something harmful to data, such as accidentally
updating or deleting data or worse, performing

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.850
malicious acts on data.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.930
The REVOKE statement revokes permissions on
an object.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.119
I have the GRANT statement up that we used
in the previous video to give the procTester

00:00:26.119 --> 00:00:31.269
account execute privileges on the GetDepartment
stored procedure.

00:00:31.269 --> 00:00:34.750
The REVOKE statement is similar to the GRANT
statement.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:41.750
I will just replace the word GRANT with REVOKE,
replace WITH GRANT OPTION with CASCADE as

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:48.760
that is needed to eliminate the grant option,
and run this statement.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:53.520
We see the message that the command completed
successfully and the permission has been revoked

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.800
from this account.

